## 2. Password Hashing

**Package**: `bcryptjs` (pure JavaScript, no native compilation required — easier on Windows dev environments).

**Strategy**:
- Hash password in a Mongoose **pre-save hook** on the User model.
- Salt rounds: `12` (high enough security, acceptable performance).
- The hook only runs if `password` is **modified** — avoids re-hashing on unrelated document saves.
- Comparison via `bcryptjs.compare(plainText, hash)` during login.

> [!NOTE]
> **Why a pre-save hook?** It centralizes hashing logic in the model so no controller can accidentally save a plain-text password. The rule: the model protects the data, the controller handles the flow.

