## 9. Request / Response Structure

### Register Request Body
```json
{
  "name": "Ayush Sharma",
  "email": "ayush@example.com",
  "password": "MySecurePass123",
  "role": "customer"
}
```

### Login Request Body
```json
{
  "email": "ayush@example.com",
  "password": "MySecurePass123"
}
```

### Success Response (Register / Login)
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Logged in successfully",
  "data": {
    "user": {
      "_id": "...",
      "name": "Ayush Sharma",
      "email": "ayush@example.com",
      "role": "customer",
      "isActive": true,
      "createdAt": "..."
    }
  }
}
```
> [!IMPORTANT]
> `password` is **never** returned. The cookie is set via `res.cookie(...)`, not in the response body.

### Error Response
```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Invalid email or password"
}
```
Handled by the centralized `errorHandler` middleware already in place from Phase 0.

