## 11. Error Handling

Reuse the existing `errorHandler` and `notFound` middlewares from Phase 0. No changes needed to those.

### HTTP Status Code Conventions

| Scenario | Status Code |
| :--- | :--- |
| Validation failure | `400 Bad Request` |
| Invalid credentials | `401 Unauthorized` |
| Role not permitted / banned | `403 Forbidden` |
| Resource not found | `404 Not Found` |
| Email already registered | `409 Conflict` |
| Server/DB error | `500 Internal Server Error` |

### Throwing errors in controllers
Use `const error = new Error('message'); error.statusCode = 403; throw error;` inside async controllers wrapped with a centralized `asyncHandler` utility — avoids `try/catch` boilerplate in every controller.

**File**: `src/utils/asyncHandler.js` — a simple wrapper: `(fn) => (req, res, next) => Promise.resolve(fn(req, res, next)).catch(next);`

